# Documentation only. Root .env and secrets/ are local and Git-ignored.
# Production settings belong to Vercel Secrets; see docs/deployment-vercel.md.
# Vercel uses Tiger PostgreSQL and ELEVENLABS_API_KEY for Scribe transcription.
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=replace-with-your-speech-to-text-enabled-key
# scripts/run_server.py loads root .env after you manually add settings; exports win.
# The Swift binary reads its environment only. This example file is never loaded directly.
# Do not export empty placeholders. See server/README.md and server/.env.example.
REVA_STORAGE=local
# REVA_HOST=127.0.0.1
# REVA_PORT=8080
# REVA_DATA_DIRECTORY=/absolute/private/demo-data
# REVA_TOKENS='{"replace-with-a-random-token-of-at-least-24-characters":"demo-user"}'
# REVA_STORAGE=postgres
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/DATABASE?sslmode=verify-full
# Tiger Cloud form (docs/tiger-setup.md); the server treats require like verify-full:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://tsdbadmin:PASSWORD@SERVICE.PROJECT.tsdb.cloud.timescale.com:PORT/tsdb?sslmode=require
# Accounts and sessions (server names, defaults shown). PostgreSQL mode or a non-loopback
# listener needs REVA_TOKENS or REVA_ACCOUNTS=enabled.
# REVA_ACCOUNTS=enabled
# REVA_SIGNUP=open
# REVA_SESSION_DAYS=30
# REVA_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://your-project.vercel.app
# disabled removes /v1/auth/*; closed answers 403 to sign-up; 1-365 days; exact origins, comma-separated, never *.
# scripts/tiger_provision.py reads these from the exported environment only, never from this file:
# TIGERDATA_ACCESS_KEY=replace-with-your-tiger-cloud-access-key
# TIGERDATA_SECRET_KEY=replace-with-your-tiger-cloud-secret-key
# TIGERDATA_PROJECT_ID=replace-with-your-tiger-cloud-project-id
# Web build setting for the Vercel project (not a server variable): VITE_REVA_API_ORIGIN=https://your-api-host
# Optional working provider adapters. Export only fields you configure manually.
# Provider access requires an explicit private REVA_TOKENS mapping above;
# the public local demo token cannot activate paid features even if keys exist.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=replace-with-your-google-ai-studio-key
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-flash-lite-latest
# All Gemini analysis uses this moving Flash-Lite alias unless a different explicit model is configured.
# Empty values and prior gemini-3.8-flash / gemini-3.5-flash-lite pins migrate to this alias.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=replace-with-your-openai-key
# OPENAI_TRANSCRIPTION_MODEL=whisper-1
# iOS explicit demo server URL/token are entered in Profile > Developer server connection.
# Server secrets must never be bundled into the iOS app.
